          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_worked_examples",
          "description": "docs/mixed-onroad.md §6.1 and §6.2, at the stages a wrong factor shows up at. travelFraction[21, 40] normalised over the whole HPMS group is 1.609175e-03; over source type 21 alone it is 4.10e-03 and every row is 2.55x high. averageSpeed is the ARITHMETIC mean, 48.185058 for the weekday; the harmonic mean gives 34.98 and S8 divides by the result. The three `sho` values are the snapshot's own `sho` table, to its six stored significant figures, at ageID 0, 20 and 40.\n\nRE-ADDRESSED FOR THE ONE-DAY RUN, BY KEY (docs/esm-conventions.md §40, §42). `activity_rows` is (day, age) with the day OUTERMOST, so it was 2 x 41 and is now 1 x 41: every ordinal above 41 moved down by 41 and every ordinal at or below 41 named a WEEKEND row that no longer exists. The weekend claims -- averageSpeed 66.094076, sho 4.88065 at the oldest cohort and 54.7283 at the newest -- are gone with it, and the weekday values that were asserted at 42 and 62 are asserted at 1 and 21. travelFraction is day-INDEPENDENT, so its two assertions keep both their ordinals and their values, which is the check that the re-addressing did not silently move a claim as well as an address.",
